    {
      "texts": [
        {
          "evidences": [
            {
              "evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269",
              "source": "PubMed",
              "id": "20133749"
            },
            {
              "evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269",
              "source": "PubMed",
              "id": "30591587"
            }
          ],
          "value": "The N-terminus (residues 1-164) forms a trimer with a partially blocked channel forms at the trimer interface (PubMed:20133749). The C-terminus has 4 domains that resemble the small subunit of RuBisCO (rbcS) joined by flexible linkers; the first one (CcmMS1) has been crystallized and folds much like RbcS. CcmMS1 binds to holo-RuBisCO (RbcL(8)-RbcS(8)), a CcmMS1-CcmMS2 constructs binds about 10-fold better, while the entire C-terminus with all 4 CcmMS domains binds with an intermediate affinity. CcmMS1 binds to a different region of RbcL than does RbcS, up to 5 CcmMS1 domains can bind to the intact holo enzyme (PubMed:30591587)"
        }
      ],
      "commentType": "DOMAIN"
    },
